.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-REVOKE-NAMESPACE-ACCESS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-revoke-namespace-access \- revoke a user's access to a namespace within an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam revoke-namespace-access
.BR \-\-user | \-u
.I ERN
.BR \-\-account\-id | \-a
.I ACCOUNTID
.BR \-\-namespace | \-s
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Revokes a user's access to one namespace within one account via the eam
service's
.I revoke-namespace-access
action.
.PP
The caller must be a global administrator, or already hold account-scoped
administrator privileges on \fIACCOUNTID\fR.
.PP
Only the named namespace is revoked - any other namespaces the user was
granted within the same account (or other accounts) are unaffected. If
this was the user's only granted namespace in the account, the account
grant itself is removed rather than left empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIERN\fR
ERN of the user to revoke access from. Required.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account\-id " " \fIACCOUNTID\fR
Account the namespace belongs to. Required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-namespace " " \fINAME\fR
Namespace within \fIACCOUNTID\fR to revoke access from. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The grant was revoked.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller
lacks administrator privileges on the account, the user does not exist,
or the user does not hold this grant. If the failure was an expired or
invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed;
run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam revoke-namespace-access \e
    --user ern:euclid:eam:eu-central-1:123456789012:user:jdoe \e
    --account-id 123456789012 --namespace development
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-namespace (1)
